<p>Authentication answers one question: is this person who they claim to be. What they're then allowed to do
lives in <a href="/toolkit/authorization">Authorization</a>. Pop splits the first question across two components —
<code>pop-auth</code> holds a file adapter and a JWT adapter, and <code>pop-db</code> holds the record class that authenticates
against a users table.</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
